cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this corpus, cite it as below. The transcripts themselves are the
  Argentine Senate's and are cited separately, by sitting date and the
  per-sitting URL in raw_data_manifest.csv; see README.md.
title: >-
  Argentine Senate stenographic transcripts, 1998–2026: a speaker-attributed
  corpus
abstract: >-
  Every stenographic record (versión taquigráfica) the Argentine Senate serves
  for its sittings from February 1998 to September 2026, parsed from the
  chamber's own PDFs and, for most of 1998-2003, its HTML export into
  speaker-attributed passages: 817 sittings, 440,445 rows, 244,624 passages of
  speech and 69,290 typed stenographer's notes, 25.28 million words of speech.
  Each passage carries the printed speaker label, the senator it resolves to
  and the caucus that senator sat with on the day. The source files are not
  redistributed: a manifest identifies each one by SHA-256 and source URL, and
  the bundled downloader fetches them again. What the project adds (the
  structure, speakers, caucuses, annotations and reference tables) is CC BY
  4.0 and the code is MIT; the text of the record is the Senate's and is not
  relicensed.
type: dataset
repository-code: https://github.com/jpripamonti/ar_congress
version: 0.5.8
date-released: '2026-09-25'
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
authors:
